id: magical-materialization
name: Magical Materialization
uaType: magical
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
tpCost: 10
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 6
# The Effect: a Basic Item, a piece of Apparel or a Weapon made with a Use Magic Check at its Craft DC one
# Category higher - picked when it is used (use-maneuver.mjs askMaterialize).
materializes: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Conjure a Basic Item, a piece of Apparel or a Weapon: Use Magic at its Craft DC one Category higher, gone at
  the end of the Combat Encounter unless a Karma Point keeps it. Passive: the Create Maneuver with Use Magic,
  and a quick one for its KP.
text: >
  Magical Materialization: You are capable of conjuring objects out of thin air, allowing you to manifest
  anything you desire, within a limit.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 6(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: You gain access to the Create Maneuver (see — Crafting) and may use your Use Magic Skill
  instead of the Craft Skill for its effects. When using the Create Maneuver to create a Basic Item, Weapon,
  or Apparel, you can spend the Ki Point Cost of Magical Materialization to reduce the Time Cost to 1 Minute,
  but increase the Difficulty Category by 1 Category (or reduce your Dice Score by 4 if the Difficulty
  Category was Grandmaster) and you do not gain a Blueprint from that use of the Create Maneuver.
  –Effect: Select either a Basic Item that does not have the [Tech] or [Food] tag, a piece of Apparel, or a
  Weapon. Roll the Craft Skill Check for your choice, using the Use Magic Skill instead of the relevant Craft
  Specialization, but increase the Difficulty Category by 1. If you fail, you do not create the item, but
  you still lose the Ki Points. If you succeed, you create the selected Item.

  The created item is either made in your hand, or in a Square within your Melee Range. Any Item made by
  Magical Materialization is destroyed at the end of a Combat Encounter, unless you spend a Karma Point to
  preserve that Item (if you created multiple Items, each Item requires a Karma Point to be preserved).

  You cannot Integrate any Items created through Magical Materialization, nor can you create any Accessory
  with a Craft DC of Grandmaster.

---

# The Passive Bonus is the Create Maneuver's (traits/adventuring/create.dbu `grantedBy`): offered to whoever
# has this, Use Magic in place of Craft where they pick it, and the quick Create - its KP paid, 1 Minute, one
# Category harder, no Blueprint.
#
# The Effect, used: what to make, the Check at its Craft DC one Category higher (Use Magic in place of Craft;
# a [Med] Basic Item's Medicine and a [Food] one's Cooking stay theirs - the user's ruling), and the card's
# Made it or Failed it. A Basic Item made is given as the Gear tab gives one, marked Materialized; a Weapon or
# a piece of Apparel is said on the card (the user's ruling). Its KP is spent either way.
#
# The table's: where it appears, the end of the Combat Encounter and its Karma Points - the Item is marked,
# not destroyed (the user's ruling) - and Integration, which is not built.
